    :slice-b2b "DONE 2026-09-01 by claude-20. LEDGER AND REGISTRY ONLY -- no src/ change, so the RUN8/S3 gate is untouched and the live wiring is NOT taken ahead of RUN7 being read, which (b2a) said must not happen. This slice pays the two debts (b2a) recorded as still owed by (b2): naming the ln E placement the live path takes, and naming the fallback for a tick whose gamma could not be solved. Both are named BEFORE any wiring is written, which is the order slice-b1 and RUN8 :acceptance both require. (1) PLACEMENT: :habit-prior-in-both, the SPM code form (spm_MDP_VB_X.m:964). This is NOT a new decision and no ruling is written: it is the arm aif-equations.edn :choices :pi-zero-form already carried as :interim and :ships-behind-flag, and that entry STAYS :open-branches. What changed is its ground. The entry said the arms could not be separated on any recorded field because ln E is absent from selection; that is false, and C23 withdraws it -- the beta solve builds its own pi and pi_0 from ln E (run7_beta_arms.clj:42-53,95) and never touches the selection posterior, so what separates the arms is whether ln E is non-uniform over the aligned field, not whether selection reads it. On S2 it is non-uniform on every tick (3 distinct values, spread 3.0445 nats, no zeros, :habit-prior-source :learned-frequency) while :habit-prior-applied? is false on 20/20 decisions. So the arms have been run, on our own field, and the near-cancellation the interim was argued from is now measured: gamma at tick 20 moves 0.004440 from the ln-E-free arm under :both against 0.062738 under :pi-only, 14.1x further. That is why the live path takes :both. It is still not ADJUDICATED -- no number here says which arm is better -- so the choice point stays open and the live wiring ships the interim behind the flag, as the registry already says. (2) FALLBACK, and it has two halves. HOLD: a tick whose solve did not BOTH converge and bracket gets no gamma-derived tau; its tau is the carried beta, which is