6 REPLACES :action with the strategic selector's pick, which is handed only :scheduler-habit-ranking and a trace id. All 20 S2 records carry :selection-boundary :reason-bearing-strategic-policy and :habit-prior-applied? false. So S3 as written would change the recorded :tau and :softmax-weights and not the action. WHAT I DID NOT ESTABLISH, and it must not be read as established: whether anything downstream of the decision map consumes :tau or :softmax-weights. I did not audit that; RUN8 must, rather than treating this as a claim that nothing does. (4) WHAT I CHECKED, so the review is auditable: re-ran run7_beta_arms.clj against the S2 trace at f625754 -- output byte-identical to the committed ARMS.txt, all 308 lines, and its own src-vs-local solver control reads delta 0.0 (ARMS.txt:2); measured ln E directly off the trace on ticks 1, 10 and 20 of 20 usable fields rather than taking RUN7's word for it; read :selection-boundary, :habit-prior-applied?, :tau, :tau-spread and :beta-source off all 20 records; read the four code sites above. Registry edit recorded as C23. p4ng negative_controls PASS (16 negative, 10 positive) and pointer_check 226 pointers 0 unresolved before the commit. RUN7 remains :done-unreviewed and nothing here reviews it."
   :slice-b2a "DONE, reviewed by claude-20 2026-09-01. futon2 4625524 (codex-21) + cf5c7de (pin repair) + f4c8f9e (control broadened). converge-beta takes :log-priors and :log-prior-placement of :none | :pi | :both, DEFAULT :none, so a reader that did not ask for ln E does not move. :pi is friston2017.txt:684 as printed; :both is spm_MDP_VB_X.m:964, the implementation form. This is the :choices :pi-zero-form choice point becoming RUNNABLE rather than being decided; no ruling is written anywhere by this slice. Pure: carry-beta, war_machine.clj and trace.clj are untouched, so the FUTON_WM_BETA_DARK path is unchanged and nothing consumes the new option. THE TEST I MOST WANTED IS THERE AND I DID NOT HAVE TO ASK FOR IT: three-log-prior-arms-are-distinct-on-field-shaped-input-test asserts three distinct betas from the three placements. The arms are measured where they DIFFER, not at a point where they coincide -- the AGENTS.md rule, applied by the author unprompted. Uniform-lnE-is-a-no-op and shift-invariance are also pinned, so the no-op cases are proven rather than assumed. Five explicit validation errors, including :log-priors supplied with :none placement. clj-kondo 0 errors 0 warnings, check-parens OK, and the tests re-run at HEAD by me: policy-precision 25 tests / 138 assertions, war-machine + trace 75 tests / 294 assertions, 0 failures 0 errors; negative_controls PASS (16 negative, 10 positive); pointer_check 218 pointers, 0 unresolved. THE STRONGEST CHECK IS ONE NO DELIVERED TEST COULD MAKE, because it needs the run artifacts: src two new arms REPRODUCE RUN7 PUBLISHED GAMMAS EXACTLY, over the 20 carried ticks of the real S2 field, against a solver that is not the one under test -- run7_beta_arms.clj carries its own bisection, written before this change and untouched by it. Carried from beta_0 = 1.0 over runs/2026-09-01-s2/wm-trace-s2.edn: :none 0.9667979197554702, :pi 0.9040600731260442, :both 0.9712374387398894, each delta 0.00e+00 against runs/2026-09-01-s2/ARMS.txt:169,216,263, 20/20 converged and bracketed in every arm. So this is the same object the arms measured, not a second implementation agreeing to four decimals -- and the :none arm reproducing the run own recorded betas is a second, on-real-data proof that the default path did not move. The arms differ by about 7% in gamma on real field data. THREE REVIEW FINDINGS, all fixed rather than re-belled. (1) cf5c7de: the default-path control anchored to e9bcf35, P-organise-the-library from an UNRELATED LANE -- whatever happened to be HEAD when the work started. Its content for this file is byte-identical to RUN7 commit, so the control gave the right answer, but the anchor names nothing a reader can interpret. That is the moving-anchor finding from the RUN5 review returning as HEAD-at-dispatch instead of HEAD~, in a repo where 039b0b8 had just pinned the sibling controls to 183749a for exactly this reason. Repinned to 039b0b8, the commit whose default path this control claims is unmoved, with the reason in the def. (2) f4c8f9e: that identity control ran on ONE input, so it would have passed while any other branch drifted. Broadened to five classes -- both solvers, a bound cut short, an unbracketed root, a two-candidate field -- with an assertion that the five really are distinct states (some converged, some not, one hit-bound, one unbracketed), so the class list cannot rot into five runs of the same thing. (3) f4c8f9e: the cross-solver agreement test covered :pi only; :both is the SPM form and the likelier candidate for the live wiring, so it now runs under both placements. PACKET CORRECTION for future dispatches: this repo :test alias uses :exec-fn, so clojure -M:test -n <ns> treats -n as a filename. The working form is clojure -X:test :nses [<ns>]. My packet specified the wrong one, from the AGENTS.md test section that is written for futon3c, and codex-21 caught it. A COLLISION ON THIS ROW, worth recording because it is the shared-repository hazard arriving in the ledge