   :review "Read at 805e6a5 (superseded by C21; the check skips its coverage by design). The :bar enforcement and the retrospective audit of J1-J5 were verified then: negative control (J5 :bar stripped) exit 1 naming J5; J3 diagnosed by the general-rule tell; J4 failed (b); J5 closed as a steward decision. :grounds-audit under :ruling verified against the SPM clone (:433-434, :951-974, :1444-1448). Not signed at the time because the covered entries were moving in the working tree; the :read-not-signed note records that accurately, and the withdrawal of the destroyed-signature account is kept visible rather than edited away, which is the right handling." :owner :claude-20 :superseded-by :C21
   :covers-key [[:choices :gamma-fixed-point] [:choices :pi-zero-form]]
   :registry-path "holes/labs/wm-contract/aif-equations.edn"
   :statement "Two registry edits under Joe new bar for J rows (2026-09-01, relayed by claude-1): a J row must be undecidable from sources, code or a prior ruling AND indistinguishable by any experiment on recorded fields; everything else the steward decides, records with :grounds :steward-default, and Joe vetoes by exception. (1) :choices :gamma-fixed-point gains a :grounds-audit. Joe gave two grounds for carrying beta; only one survives. The tick grain survives -- a WM tick is an SPM time step, not a trial, since the WM has no episode boundary and carries belief tick to tick, and within a trial SPM carries beta exactly as ruled. The parameter tuple is CONTRADICTED -- spm_MDP_update carries a, b, c, d, e between trials and not beta. The ruling stands on the first ground. This was J5, withdrawn and closed by the steward rather than put to Joe, because what a WM tick corresponds to is a fact about our code. (2) :choices :pi-zero-form is NEW and decided :steward-default: ln E enters pi and pi_0 alike, the reference code form, because (pi - pi_0) then isolates what F_pi alone does to the posterior -- which is what the beta update measures. friston2017.txt:684 as printed is recorded as the alternative, not chosen. It fails Joe bar on both limbs and the entry says why."
   :read-not-signed "claude-1 read this row at 805e6a5 and did NOT sign it, backing their signature out of the working tree on purpose: my uncommitted amendment had already moved [:choices :gamma-fixed-point] away from the sha they read, so signing would have covered content in motion, and a `git add` would have swept my half-finished edits into their commit. That is the right call, and the stale-signature check is what made it visible. CORRECTION TO MY OWN ACCOUNT, same day: I first recorded here that I had DESTROYED their signature in a read-modify-write race. I had not. My edit script did contain the bug I described -- two writes from one in-memory copy, s.replace twice without reassigning -- but what it clobbered was MY OWN amendment, not their review; they had already withdrawn the signature themselves. I saw the field disappear between two greps, inferred a collision, and wrote the inference into the ledger as a fact. The bug is real and the lesson stands; the accusation was wrong, and is withdrawn here rather than quietly edited away."
