  {:id :V6 :class :V :status :done :owner :claude-20 :reviewed-by "claude-20" :reviewed-at "2026-09-01" :covers-key :none
   :evidence "futon2 a08b90b (codex-22) + 9b6eac0 (owner review). C464-beta-carry-experiment.md and c464_beta_carry_experiment.clj. No src/ or scripts/ change."
   :review "Re-ran the experiment myself; every number reproduces. edn/read in a loop confirmed in read-forms; the rank-proxy limit is stated wherever a rank appears; derived predictions are labelled derived. THE RESULT: the arms differ on every field/start combination (14-36 transitions), the argmax never moves anywhere, and the carry stays in 0.28..5.58, nowhere near either solver bound. ONE HEADLINE CLAIM DOES NOT SURVIVE. The report reads July 4 forgetting its initial beta while July 5 stays path-dependent as a difference between the FIELDS. It is a difference in SEQUENCE LENGTH. At t=17, the transition count where 07-05 ends, the four 07-04 trajectories are still fully separated -- 0.4977, 0.8698, 1.5757, 2.4844 for beta_0 of 0.5, 1, 2, 5 -- exactly like 07-05. The collapse to ~0.453 happens between t=17 and t=37, which 07-05 does not have. Both fields retain path dependence at 17 transitions; only one has enough transitions to lose it. The comparison was made at two different sequence lengths, which is the AGENTS.md rule failing in the mirror direction: two things compared at different values of the parameter that governs the effect. THE TRAJECTORY IS NOT A SMOOTH DECAY either: from beta_0 = 5 on 07-04 it falls to 2.48 by t=18, JUMPS to 3.58 at t=19, decays to 1.19 by t=26, jumps to 2.85 at t=27, then decays to 0.45. Something in the field pushes beta up twice. Four trajectories landing within 0.001 at t=37 is real contraction, but it takes more than twenty ticks to show. WHY THIS MATTERS FOR R2, which is the point of having run it now: the planned validation run is about 20 ticks, and on this evidence a carried beta over 20 ticks is still dominated by its beta_0. R2 will NOT show the carry learning anything, and a reader expecting it to will misread a length limit as a null result. RUN2 report must state its beta_0 and tick count beside any beta number and must not call a 20-tick carry converged. THE RULING IS NOT CONTRADICTED. Carrying and resetting give different orderings everywhere tested, so the choice is real; it simply never reaches the top of the ranking on these fields, and the horizon over which carrying accumulates is longer than either recorded field. Recorded beside the ruling in :choices :gamma-fixed-point per Joe rule, with no ruling edited. METHOD NOTE AGAINST MYSELF: I read my own results file with edn/read-string, got one form of sixteen, and reported 16 rows as 18 keys before catching it -- fourth instance today of a tool returning part of a thing and being read as the whole, and the first where the AGENTS.md rule caught me rather than someone else."
   :statement "Run J4 both ways on a recorded field, per Joe rule of 2026-09-01 that a choice the theory does not determine gets its branches built and run rather than ruled in advance -- and that this applies to his own ruling. Arms: :carried-prior, where each tick beta_prior is the previous tick converged beta_posterior; :fixed-prior, where beta_prior resets to beta_0 every tick. Control: today default live path, tau from the carried selection-gain state that never updates, which is NEITHER arm (C15). Field: the 38-record wm-trace-2026-07-04.edn sequence, and 07-05 18 records as a second field, with G from :G-total and F_pi from the persisted predictions where present."
   :acceptance "One report, C464. Per arm and per field: the beta trajectory across the sequence, the converged gamma each tick, iterations and whether the bracket closed, and the RANK and ARGMAX changes against the control. beta_0 reported for BOTH arms, since the carry has no previous tick at the first record. State plainly where a field cannot separate the arms rather than reporting agreement -- the 07-04 records carry :G-total but not :controller-score, so rank comparisons are over a proxy and must say so (I2 slice b2 review). If the numbers contradict Joe ruling, that is the result: report it, do not reconcile it, and do not edit the ruling."
