   :review "THE ANSWER IS NOT SAFE TO RUN, which is the answer I asked for and the right one. Verified the load-bearing claim myself rather than taking it: war_machine.clj:4844-4854 POSTs /api/alpha/portfolio/step from inside judge, UNCONDITIONALLY -- wrapped in try/catch, which swallows the error but does not prevent the call, and carrying {\"emit-evidence\":false}, which limits what it emits but still runs an AIF step on the futon3c portfolio engine. A validation run of 20 ticks would step that engine 20 times. ONE DETAIL THE REPORT DID NOT DRAW, and it makes the fix easy: a read-only path already exists in the same file. scan-portfolio (war_machine.clj:2202-2212) takes a step? parameter DEFAULTING TO FALSE and documents GET /api/alpha/portfolio/state as the non-stepping call. The judge code does not use it; it POSTs directly. So the capability is there and unused at this site. THE 14/4 SPLIT IS HONEST AND THE SHAPE MATTERS: most of the effects without a disabling mechanism are full-loop only -- agency bells that let agents edit and commit, status mutation, phase and run receipt files, cancellation POSTs -- and the diagnostic entrypoint does not enter the full loop. Confirmed: scripts/futon2/run_tick_once.clj contains no reference to full_loop_runner. So the diagnostic path has exactly ONE unsafe actuator, and it is the portfolio POST. R2 STAYS BLOCKED. Opened R5 to suppress the POST on the diagnostic path; RUN2 unblocks when that lands and I have read it, not before. codex-21 answering NOT SAFE rather than producing a confident command is the outcome the packet was written to make possible, and it is worth saying that a discovery which stops the campaign is a successful discovery." :assigned "2026-09-01, dispatched to codex-21. Discovery only, no run."
