   :review "THE SUPPRESSION IS STRUCTURAL, not a flag someone checks: portfolio-step-for-judge is (if-not step? {absence} (try POST ...)), so with step? false the POST is in an unreachable branch. Option :step-portfolio?, default TRUE, so production is unchanged; run_tick_once.clj passes false. THE INJECTION TEST IS REAL and does what the packet demanded: with-redefs on http/post to a fn that THROWS, then assert the result equals {:status :absent :reason :portfolio-step-suppressed}. If the POST were reached the throw would be swallowed by the historical catch-all into nil, and nil is not the absence map, so the test fails. That is a proof of no-call rather than an inspection of a branch. THE ABSENCE IS HANDLED, NOT JUST PRODUCED -- I checked the consumers rather than the producer. mission-priorities reads it through get-in with [] defaults (war_machine.clj:4284-4285), so it degrades exactly as the old nil did; and the :portfolio-recommendation cond at :4924-4931 tests (= :absent (:status portfolio-step)) FIRST and propagates the absence, so a suppressed tick records why the recommendation is missing instead of shaping {:action nil :recommendation nil} that reads like a present-but-empty answer. Suppressed and failed are also distinguishable downstream: absence map versus nil. ONE REVIEW FINDING, fixed: THE CROSS-VERSION CONTROL DECAYED. It began as HEAD~, which the shared checkout broke when an unrelated commit landed between; codex-20 fixed that by anchoring to the parent of the LATEST commit touching war_machine.clj. That survives concurrency but rots -- after the next edit to this file that parent already contains R5 change, so the control compares R5 default path with itself, and the claim it backs quietly turns from the default preserves pre-suppression behaviour into the last commit changed nothing. Both are checks; only one is the claim R5 makes. Pinned to e7a9bb6^ with the reasoning in the def. A control for a fixed claim gets a fixed anchor. R2 IS NOW UNBLOCKED -- on my having READ the suppression, which is what the row required, not on a report saying it is fixed." :assigned "2026-09-01, dispatched to codex-20, after R1 found the one unsafe actuator on the diagnostic path."
   :statement "war_machine.clj:4844-4854 POSTs /api/alpha/portfolio/step from inside judge, unconditionally. A 20-tick validation run would step the futon3c portfolio inference engine 20 times, which is a real side effect on another service. Make it suppressible, and have the diagnostic entrypoint suppress it."
