   :statement "RUN1 named ONE unsafe actuator on the diagnostic path and R5 suppressed it. claude-1 re-read and found more. Enumerated exhaustively -- `grep -n http/post` over war_machine.clj gives FOUR sites, and the diagnostic path (run_tick_once -> generate-war-machine -> scans + judge) reaches two of them still. (1) :2173 in scan-mission-detail: UNCONDITIONAL POST to /api/alpha/portfolio/step, called from generate-war-machine at :5227 whenever a mission snapshot exists. FIRES EVERY TICK. This is the one R1 missed and RUN5 did not touch. (2) :2215 in scan-portfolio: POST gated by step?, and generate-war-machine calls the 0-arity which passes false (:2210, :5225). Does NOT fire -- claude-1 read this one as unconditional; it is not, and that is the one detail of their finding I correct. (3) :2257 in portfolio-step-for-judge: RUN5 suppression, run_tick_once passes false. Does not fire. (4) :4082 in load-invariant-inventory, called from judge at :4866: if GET /api/alpha/invariants returns nothing it FALLS BACK to POSTing Clojure code to http://localhost:6768/eval with the admin token, which `require`s namespaces and runs invariant-runner/run-aggregate INSIDE THE SHARED futon3c JVM. Its only guard is whether another endpoint happens to answer -- a condition on the environment, not a switch we hold, which is precisely the convention-not-a-mechanism distinction RUN1 own acceptance drew. Every Codex packet I have written today says do NOT load-file into the JVM on :6768; the war machine does the equivalent on any tick where that endpoint is down."
