   :result "REPRODUCED BY A SOLVER THAT IS NOT THE ONE THAT RAN. run7_beta_arms.clj carries its own bisection -- it has to, since converge-beta cannot put ln E in pi_0 -- checked against converge-beta first (delta 0.0) and then reproducing all twenty recorded betas from their recorded priors at delta 0.00e+00. THE J4 ARMS, on :controller-score rather than the G-total proxy C464 was confined to, and on PERSISTED predictions rather than reconstructed ones: carry and reset differ and the difference NEVER REACHES THE ARGMAX -- 0 of 20 ticks at every beta_0 in {0.5, 1, 2, 5}. All rank movement is at beta_0 = 0.5, up to 42 of 145 ranks (max move 41); at 1, 2 and 5 no rank moves at all. So C464's answer survives being re-asked on the machine's own rank. DIRECTION DEPENDS ON beta_0 -- up at 0.5, 1.0 and 2.0, DOWN at 5.0 -- so the carry contracts toward a value inside (0.5, 5.0) rather than running away, and no floor or ceiling is approached. BUT NOTHING HERE IS CONVERGED (C22): the 0.5 and 5.0 arms close 1.3% of their 4.5 gap in twenty ticks. THE PI_0 ARMS: the choice I1(b1) recorded as one that 'does not bite on the live path today' DOES bite, by a factor of three. gamma at t=20 is 0.9668 with ln E in neither (what the run computed), 0.9041 with it in pi only (friston2017.txt:684), 0.9712 with it in both (spm_MDP_VB_X.m:964). The SPM code form sits closest to the ln-E-free one because (pi - pi_0) cancels E -- which is exactly the ground claude-1 gave for choosing it, now measured rather than reasoned. ln E is available as :habit-prior-bias (efe.clj:896) on 20/20 records, :habit-prior-source :learned-frequency throughout. NO RULING WRITTEN: this is evidence for the (b2) row that will make one. AND A MEASUREMENT WHOSE FIRST FORM WOULD HAVE MISLED: the dark posterior's argmax is the machine's RANK 134 OF 145 on every tick. Comparing the two SPREADS (G 125.34 against F_pi 0.7540) would have supported 'F_pi cannot move the answer'; that is the tail's property, and among the leaders the gap is dG +0.3168 against dF -0.5634, so F_pi wins there. This bounds S4 (RUN9, live F_pi in the posterior), NOT S3 -- S3 changes gamma in sigma(-gamma G) and adds no F_pi term, and the S3-relevant number is that at gamma near 1 the carry moves no ranks over 20 ticks. The field is NOT frozen despite these summaries being constant to four decimals: all 20 G vectors and all 20 F_pi vectors are pairwise distinct and 18 of 20 observations are distinct."
   :defect-found "THE PRE-FLIGHT STRANDED THE RUN LOCK IT IS A PRE-FLIGHT FOR, and the first S2 attempt was refused by it. r6_zero_post_preflight.clj intercepts spit so a tick leaves no artifact; wm-run-lock/acquire! (RUN12) takes the lock by .createNewFile then spitting the holder record, and release! deletes the file only when it reads its own token back out of it. With the write intercepted the lock file stayed ZERO BYTES, release read :not-ours, and the file survived -- exactly the state RUN12 fails closed on ('a lock file with no pid is what an acquirer looks like between creating the file and writing it'). So every run after any pre-flight would have been refused, by a lock nobody held. The two mechanisms had never met: RUN12 ran no tick, and every pre-flight before it predates the lock. Fixed in ed2be78 -- run-lock writes pass through, so a pre-flight tick holds and releases the lock like the tick it is, and the pre-flight now reports lock writes separately and prints whether the lock is released when it exits. Verified: the repaired pre-flight ran, printed 'run lock after the tick: released', and the run then took the lock."
