present REFUSES (adapters/fulab.clj:262-321): :chosen nil, :refused? true, and NO :tau, :logits or :probs, all three of which the pre-AC7 code reported off the substituted zero. With a caller-supplied :chosen, with no candidates, or in either update-beliefs branch (adapters/fulab.clj:323-374), tau is a diagnostic nobody branches on: the derived value is OMITTED and nothing is blocked -- the pattern-action branch still updates its evidence counts (AC2's reject-the-member-not-the-collection). The record reports the absence either way, carrying :required?. MEASURED BOTH DIRECTIONS against the pre-AC7 namespace loaded into one process, on {:candidates [:a :b]} with no surplus: pre-AC7 chose :a at tau 1.0 with probs {:a 0.5 :b 0.5} and sampled? true; post-AC7 chooses NOTHING and emits the :absent record. ON THE HEALTHY PATHS NOTHING MOVED: four contexts (surplus 1.0; surplus 0.0; surplus 0.0 with :chosen; empty candidate set) give :aif maps EQUAL to pre-AC7 once the two added keys (:refused?, :temperature-events) are removed, and the generic update-beliefs branch is equal likewise (surplus 2.0, tau 1/3). One rewrite was REVERTED during the row for exactly that reason -- (and (some? sampled) ...) changed a reported :sampled? from nil to false on three of the four. PERSISTENCE: every result carries :aif :temperature-events (adapters/fulab.clj:190-199), the present-only projection, empty exactly when the surplus was read. There is no further carrier and that is a fact about the site: C226 found NO in-repository call site constructing this adapter, so there is nothing between it and trace.clj to project through; the seam is typed exactly so a later connection can neither fabricate a temperature nor clamp a signed epsilon on its way in. GATES: clj-kondo 0 errors 0 warnings on the two changed files; check-parens OK on both; clojure -M:test -m cognitect.test-runner -d test/futon2 1025 tests / 6381 assertions / 0 failures / 0 errors (was 1017/6312 at AC6: +8 deftests, +69 assert