   :statement "The selector consult (Joe 2026-09-02: 'another example of recorded but never consulted, written but never wired'). U1's readiness work established (SPEC-dormant-wiring.md U1 READINESS point 4) that flipping the flags changes the RECORDED posterior, not the CHOSEN action: :selection-boundary :strategic-recommendation chooses the head of the G-ordered list (policy.clj:499) and records the F_pi-bearing posterior at :551 unread; the :actuation boundary selects by ln E - G/tau (policy.clj:696) but f-pi-opts reaches only strategic-recommendation (policy.clj:491), so F_pi never enters a selection on either path. Build the selector change: a selection mode in which the chosen action IS the argmax of the full-score posterior (ln E - G/tau_eff - F_pi), behind a declared input (env or opts), preconditions fail-closed as in f-pi-posterior-preconditions!. Candidates stay opaque at the seam (U5). Join F_pi by :candidate-identity, NEVER by rank/N keys (the transposition trap pinned in rank-key-join-breaks-the-replay-test)."
