   :evidence "futon2 845de41 (the test ns, the probe, its artifact, C489, and the M-zaif-harness note) and the ledger commit carrying this line. WHAT WAS BUILT: test/futon2/aif/zaif_full_loop_test.clj, 620 lines, 15 deftests / 136 assertions, ONE deftest per R node so a regression names the node. THE CROSS-REPO PROBLEM AND HOW IT IS CLOSED, because it is the first thing a reviewer will doubt: zaif v0 lives in futon3c (src/futon3c/agents/zaif_controller.clj L1-L270, zaif_inputs.clj L1-L209) and futon3c is NOT on futon2's classpath (futon2/deps.edn L1-L8, the :deps map), so a futon2 test cannot call decide(). The acceptance permits a planted fixture 'with the shape pinned against zaif_controller.clj'. The fixture's NUMBERS are not planted: they were produced by the SHIPPED controller by u6_zaif_decision.clj:1-109 running in the futon3c JVM against futon3c 0252995, frozen at U6-ZAIF-DECISION.txt (byte-identical on two consecutive runs, md5 bc7764596e6769a5928763850db93e7b). The fixture's SHAPE is re-derived from the controller SOURCE on every test run: controller-forms (zaif_full_loop_test.clj:94-104) reads the file, source-constants and source-arm-order pull the constants map and the arm vector, and zaif-fixture-shape-is-pinned-against-the-controller-source-test (:261-289) checks the fixture against both. VERIFIED BY MUTATION IN BOTH DIRECTIONS: changing the FIXTURE's operator-attention-cost 0.65 -> 0.5 turns the suite red (3 failures), and changing the SOURCE constant 0.65 -> 0.55 turns it red the same way (futon3c working tree restored to clean immediately after; git status empty). That is what z2_calibrate.clj L56-L58's self-declared inlined copy of the arithmetic does not have. THE FROZEN DECISION is a real recorded operator turn, e-ce907fcf-c7e1-4272-a4a2-13def7aaaa50 at 2026-06-08T15:26:51.274850972Z from calibration-sessions.edn: gold-judged, :is_correction true, attributed to M-futon-forward-model -- the ONE mission whose B1 gamma cell is burned in (gamma 0.70