es a basis pointer, that EXACTLY ONE node (R16) is :exercises, that R5 and R14 are :partial, and that R17 is :stub-by-design -- which is what the statement predicted. R4's stub is pinned by behaviour, not by assertion: forward_model.clj:25-31 excludes all four arms and fm/predict THROWS on each (:332-341). U5 HELD: r16-candidates-stay-opaque-at-the-seam-test (:487-512) gives the same scores, ln E and F_pi to {:type :retrieve} candidates and to :apply-cascade candidates with different targets and payloads, and gets the same chosen rank and the same :selection-law :chosen-rank, while the candidate identity does change so the test is not vacuous. SAME FUNCTIONS, NOT REIMPLEMENTATIONS: risk is pref/kl against pref/c-distribution, the same call efe.clj:659-668 makes; ambiguity is reached through #'efe/ambiguity (efe.clj:37-61), the private var efe.clj:679 itself calls -- the discipline C487 control 2 used; tau is policy/effective-temperature; ln E is habit-prior/log-priors; F_pi is policy-free-energy/f-pi-for-candidate; the posterior is policy/selection-scores and policy/softmax-weights; the choice is policy/select-action. NO RULING AND NO REGISTRY WRITE: :covers-key :none, aif-equations.edn and control-map-edges.edn are untouched (negative_controls reports shared registries untouched), and nothing is written to :choices or :decisions. Replay only -- no live run, no run lock taken, nothing under data/ written, persist-decision! never called. NOTED, NOT FIXED: pointer_check.bb's root list has no futon3c root, so this row's central file cannot be cited in file.clj:NN form here without a false 'file not found'; futon3c pointers above are written as '.clj L11-L20'. Same defect class C472/C473/AC7 named, one repo over; appending a root is a p4ng change and outside this acceptance. GATES: clj-kondo 0 errors / 0 warnings on the one changed .clj; futon4/dev/check-parens.el OK; clojure -X:test :patterns [\\\"futon2\\\\..*-test$\\\"] 1070 tests / 6890 assertions, 0 failures / 0 er